Group,

Just to follow up my previous post and close this out, there is really 
no problem
in developing PALCode on RH Linux.  One needs to do a few things:

1) use -m21164pc or whatever is appropriate on the as command line to 
get the PAL opcodes recopnized

2) use ".set nomacro" within the source to keep as from doing strange 
things with lda and ldah

3) strip the object and the file headers

The code can then be placed in memory and the old PALCode will swap in it.

I guess there is not much active PALCode development these days.

Don




